    <statement><p>Given a the vector equation 
<m>\mathbf{r} (t) = 
(-2 + 4 t) \mathbf{i}  + 
(4 + 3 t) \mathbf{j}  +
(3 + 2 t) \mathbf{k}</m>, 
rewrite this in terms of the parametric equations for the line.</p>
<p><m>x(t) =</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><m>y(t) =</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p><m>z(t) =</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-2+4t</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>4+3t</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>3+2t</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
